# Published release assets are byte-exact artifacts of a validated, sealed build. Their SHA-256
# checksums are recorded inside SHA256SUMS.txt at packaging time, so any line-ending translation on
# the way into or out of the repository makes the published checksum file disagree with the files it
# describes -- `sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS.txt` failed for release-assets.json and release-manifest.json
# on the live site for exactly this reason. Nothing under the download tree is ever converted.
docs/public/downloads/** -text
